# Git commit attribution (cloud + agent)

When committing in **this repository** (`diazMelgarejo/periscope`):

1. **Do not** add `Co-authored-by:`, `Made-with: Cursor`, or other agent trailers you author.
2. **Forbidden** co-author / author emails on fork commits: any address outside the allowlist in
   `scripts/git/check_commit_message.sh` (mirrors orama `docs/wiki/08-git-hygiene-and-branching.md`).
3. **Before** `git commit`, run `bash scripts/git/disable-cursor-commit-attribution.sh` if hooks may have been reset.
4. **Prefer** `bash scripts/git/commit-clean.sh -m "type(scope): summary"` when Cursor keeps injecting trailers.
5. Use only approved author identity: `cyre <diazMelgarejo@gmail.com>` (or `cyre <Lawrence@cyre.me>` /
   `Codex <codex@openai.com>` per `scripts/git/check_identity.sh`).
6. Once per clone: `bash scripts/git/install-local-hooks.sh`.
7. On Cursor Cloud VM boot: `bash scripts/git/apply-attribution-guards.sh`.

Canonical multi-repo policy: orama-system `docs/wiki/12-cursor-cloud-commit-attribution.md`.

Desktop (optional): Cursor Settings → Agents → Attribution → OFF (IDE/CLI only; cloud may still inject until guards run).
